   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the general municipal law, in relation to permitting the\nKenmore-Town of Tonawanda union free school district to establish an insurance\nreserve fund",
    "basePrintNo": "S1735",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S1735-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §6-n, Gen Muni L",
    "lawSection": "General Municipal Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S1735\n\nSPONSOR: JACOBS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the general municipal law, in relation to permitting the\nKenmore-Town of Tonawanda union free school district to establish an\ninsurance reserve fund\n\n \nPURPOSE OF THE BILL:\n\nThis bill would allow the Kenmore-Town of Tonawanda Union Free School\nDistrict which has elected to self-insure to establish an insurance\nreserve fund.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\n§ 1-Amends paragraph (a) of subdivision 2 of § 6-n of the General Munic-\nipal Law by providing the Kenmore-Town of Tonawanda Union Free School\nDistrict the ability to establish an insurance reserve fund.\n\n§ 2-Effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nIn order to prudently manage the rising costs of health insurance, the\nKenmore-Town of Tonawanda Union Free School District elected to self-in-\nsure its health benefit program. Self-insurance offers many advantages\nfor school districts and its employees, however under current law school\ndistricts are prevented from retaining more than four percent of their\nbudget in an unappropriated fund balance. Authorizing the Kenmore-Town\nof Tonawanda Union Free School District to establish an insurance\nreserve fund will allow them to manage year-to-year variability in\nclaims.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nS. 8245 (2017-2018) Passed Assembly\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
